    "result": "I've fixed the floating-point precision issue in three functions that convert prices to cents:\n- **parseEuros** in `src/money.js`: Now uses `Math.round()` after multiplying by 100\n- **cellCents** in `src/money.js`: Added rounding for CSV import \n- **decimalCommaToCents** in `src/locale.js`: Added rounding for European decimal format\n\nThe issue was that multiplying decimal numbers by 100 in JavaScript can produce tiny floating-point errors (like 3995.0000000000005 instead of 3995), which failed the validation check that expects whole cents.\n\nAll tests pass, and `subtrack add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03` now works correctly. Would you like me to commit these changes?",
